---
import SiteLayout from '../../layouts/SiteLayout.astro';
---
<SiteLayout title="Frequently Asked Questions | VYQDA Technologies" description="Answers about VYQDA software products, custom software development, delivery approach, ongoing support and project estimates." canonical="https://vyqda.com/faq/" active="faq">
<section class="page-hero"><div class="wrap page-hero__inner"><p class="page-eyebrow">FREQUENTLY ASKED QUESTIONS</p><h1>Useful answers before <em>the first conversation.</em></h1><p class="page-hero__lead">Every project is different. These answers explain how we approach products, custom software and ongoing technology work.</p><div class="page-hero__actions"><a class="button button--primary" href="/contact/">Discuss Your Requirements <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a><a class="button button--secondary" href="/products/">Explore Products</a></div></div></section>
<section class="content-section"><div class="wrap"><div class="faq-page-list">
<details><summary>What does VYQDA Technologies do?</summary><p>VYQDA Technologies develops software products and provides custom software development and technology services for businesses. Areas of work include web applications, SaaS product engineering, business automation, workforce tools and operational software.</p></details>
<details><summary>Does VYQDA build custom software for businesses?</summary><p>Yes. Custom projects can be scoped around business workflows, user needs, integrations and technical constraints. The best starting point is a conversation about the problem, desired outcome, scope and timeline.</p></details>
<details><summary>Does VYQDA offer ready-made software products?</summary><p>The portfolio includes Timenox, Timenox 360, Vyfoo Restaurant POS, VYQDA Retail and SHYFT Box Finder. Product capabilities and fit should be confirmed against your specific use case.</p></details>
<details><summary>Can you support an existing application after launch?</summary><p>Ongoing work may include maintenance, bug fixes, technical improvements, new features and continued development. The support arrangement depends on the application and agreed requirements.</p></details>
<details><summary>How do you estimate custom software cost?</summary><p>Cost depends on scope, integrations, complexity, delivery stages and ongoing support needs. A useful estimate starts with requirements and priorities rather than a generic price that may not fit the project.</p></details>
<details><summary>How do we start a project?</summary><p>Share a description of your business, the problem to solve, intended users, timeline and integration requirements. This helps establish whether a product, tailored solution or phased approach is the right fit.</p></details>
<details><summary>Can you work with an existing application or codebase?</summary><p>Potentially. The first step is to understand the current architecture, quality, risks, documentation and desired outcomes before recommending changes.</p></details>
<details><summary>Do you provide support after delivery?</summary><p>Post-launch support can be discussed as part of the engagement, including maintenance, fixes, feature improvements and ongoing development according to agreed scope.</p></details>
</div></div></section>
<section class="content-section"><div class="wrap"><div class="page-cta"><div><h2>Have a question specific to your project?</h2><p>Share a little context and we can discuss the best next step.</p></div><a class="button button--primary" href="/contact/">Start a Conversation <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></div></div></section>
